                          "text":  "I felt more than 1,300 of them. Each one sent waves down through the planet and back, and those waves drew a picture of the inside of Mars: crust, mantle, and a molten core.\n\nNot everything worked. I carried a heat probe called the mole that was meant to hammer itself five metres into the ground. The soil here clumped in a way nobody expected, and the mole kept popping back out. My team tried for almost two years to help it with my arm. In the end they had to stop. That is how exploring goes sometimes.",
